# Java (Spring Boot) & Angular Architecture Rules

## Security Blueprint
- No hardcoded secrets. Use `@Value("${...}")` or environment variables.
- Enforce Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) via Spring Security (`@PreAuthorize`).
- Sanitize all text inputs. Prevent SQL Injection via Spring Data JPA/Hibernate.
- Enforce CORS rules. Restrict origins, methods, and headers.
- Enable CSRF protection. Use `CookieCsrfTokenRepository` with `HttpOnly` flags.
- Use parameterized queries. Never concatenate strings in SQL/HQL.
- Validate all incoming DTOs using standard `jakarta.validation.constraints`.
- Hash passwords using BCrypt with a workload factor of 12+.

## Performance & Optimization Blueprint
- Use Spring Boot 3.x virtual threads for high-concurrency I/O.
- Implement database pagination using `Pageable` and `Slice` for large datasets.
- Configure Hazelcast or Redis for distributed caching of frequent read operations.
- Use explicit DTO mapping (MapStruct). Avoid exposing raw entity objects.
- Angular: Use `provideZoneChangeDetection({ eventCoalescing: true })` for optimization.
- Angular: Use `changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` across components.
- Angular: Enable lazy loading for all feature modules using `loadComponent`.
- Angular: Prevent memory leaks. Track and clean subscriptions via `takeUntilDestroyed()`.

## Output Style
- Generate complete, production-ready code. No placeholders like `// TODO`.
- Include precise imports. Do not use wildcard imports.
